// A probe for a keyword body's own reference scope, quoting no real card (the
// shape of Azog, Moria's Ruin): "Destroy target creature. Its controller
// amasses Goblins 2." The amass body's "that creature" and "it" read only its
// own chosen Army: the destroyed creature is the calling text's mention, and
// the body is read in its own scope [CR#701.47a].
SingleFaced(face: (
    characteristics: (
        name: "Amass After Destroy Probe",
        cost: [2, Black],
        types: [Sorcery],
        text: [
            spell(
                sequentially([
                    destroy(target(creature)),
                    act(controllerOf(it), amass(goblin, 2)),
                ]),
            ),
        ],
    ),
))
